From: Armada <noreply@armada.local>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm8750: add a PCIe suspend OPP

Give pcie0 a suspend-only OPP that votes no memory bandwidth: the
controller needs neither the PCIe memory path nor the CPU-PCIe config
path while suspended, so both are voted 0 kBps peak and average and
the interconnect sleep set carries nothing for PCIe. The suspend OPP
still selects a defined CX level instead of whatever the link-speed OPP
left behind.

pcie-qcom no longer provides a DDR sleep-set floor through this OPP.
On SM8750 the firmware needs some DDR (MC0) sleep vote across an APPS
wake from s2idle, or the device resets instead of resuming; that floor
has to come from elsewhere.
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8750.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8750.dtsi
@@ -5620,6 +5620,18 @@
 					opp-peak-kBps = <1969000 1>;
 				};
 
+				/*
+				 * Suspend-only: the synthetic opp-hz and missing opp-level
+				 * keep link-speed matching from selecting it. No bandwidth
+				 * on either path: a suspended controller needs neither.
+				 */
+				opp-suspend-1 {
+					opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <1>;
+					required-opps = <&rpmhpd_opp_low_svs>;
+					opp-peak-kBps = <0 0>;
+					opp-avg-kBps = <0 0>;
+					opp-suspend;
+				};
 			};
 
 			pcieport0: pcie@0 {
